  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when a mobile home door sticks or won't latch properly, right? Sometimes it's a simple fix, other times it hints at bigger issues. You'll want to check for obstructions first—sometimes something's just in the way. Then, take a look at the hinges. Loose screws are a common culprit, so grab a screwdriver and tighten 'em up! If it's still not right, the hinges might be out of alignment. Shims can often help here, getting everything back into place. If the door's rubbing, a little sanding on the edges can go a long way. Don't forget the weatherstripping! If it's old or damaged, replacing it can solve air leaks and sticking problems. But if you're constantly fighting with the same door, or if you see signs of water damage, it might be time to call in someone experienced. We're here to help figure out what's going on and get that door working smoothly again.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
